@startuml UC001_CreateNote_Sequence
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE

' Color palette: boundary=blue, service=green, domain=amber, repo=lavender, infra=gray
actor "User" as U
participant "«boundary»\nNoteEditor\n(note-editor.tsx)" as EDITOR #E6F0FB
participant "«boundary»\nNotes API (router.py)" as API #E6F0FB
participant "«service»\nNoteService" as NOTESERV #E7F4EA
participant "«service»\nFolderService" as FOLDERSERV #E7F4EA
participant "«repository»\nNoteRepository" as NOTEREPO #EEE7F7
database "PostgreSQL (notes)" as PGNOTES #ECECEC
database "PostgreSQL (folders)" as PGFOLDERS #ECECEC

== Phase 1: User Input ==
U    -> EDITOR : 1.1 Enter title + content, click "Save"
EDITOR -> API : 1.2 POST /api/notes\n{title, content, folder_id, JWT}
note over API : CreateNoteRequest validation (Pydantic)\n- title: required, max 255\n- content: optional, max 1MB\n- folder_id: required UUID\nIf invalid -> 422 Bad Request

== Phase 2: Authentication & Authorization ==
API  -> NOTESERV : 1.3 create_note(user_id, folder_id, title, content)\nNote: user_id extracted from verified JWT

== Phase 3: Verify Folder Ownership ==
NOTESERV -> FOLDERSERV : 2.1 get_folder(folder_id)
FOLDERSERV -> NOTEREPO : 2.2 find_by_id(folder_id)\nNote: borrows NoteRepository for query, or uses FolderRepository
alt Folder exists & belongs to user
  NOTEREPO -> PGFOLDERS : 2.3 SELECT folder WHERE folder_id = ? AND user_id = ?
  PGFOLDERS --> FOLDERSERV : Folder
  FOLDERSERV --> NOTESERV : Folder
else Folder not found or unauthorized
  PGFOLDERS --> FOLDERSERV : None
  FOLDERSERV --> NOTESERV : raise FolderNotFound
  NOTESERV --> API : FolderNotFound Exception
  API --> EDITOR : 4.1 404 "Folder not found"
  EDITOR --> U : Error message
end

== Phase 4: Create Note Aggregate ==
NOTESERV -> NOTESERV : 3.1 Create Note(note_id=UUID(), user_id, folder_id,\ntitle=Title(title), content=Content(content),\nis_pinned=false, is_deleted=false, created_at=now(), updated_at=now())
note over NOTESERV
  Title & Content are value objects (validated during construction).
  If title is empty -> ValueError raised, caught by API as 422.
end note

== Phase 5: Persist to Database ==
NOTESERV -> NOTEREPO : 3.2 save(note)
note over NOTEREPO
  Repository interface; NoteService does not know about SQL.
end note
NOTEREPO -> PGNOTES : 3.3 INSERT INTO notes\n(note_id, user_id, folder_id, title, content, is_pinned, is_deleted, created_at, updated_at)\nVALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, false, false, ?, ?)
alt INSERT succeeds
  PGNOTES --> NOTEREPO : Success (ACID transaction)
  NOTEREPO --> NOTESERV : (void)
  NOTESERV --> API : Note
else Database error (connection lost, constraint violation)
  PGNOTES --> NOTEREPO : Exception
  NOTEREPO --> NOTESERV : Exception
  NOTESERV --> API : raise PersistenceError
  API --> EDITOR : 4.2 500 "Failed to create note"
  EDITOR --> U : Error message, user retries
end

== Phase 6: Return Response ==
alt Success
  API -> API : 3.4 Convert Note → NoteDTO\n{note_id, title, content, folder_id, is_pinned, created_at, updated_at}
  API --> EDITOR : 4.1 200 OK\n{note_id, title, content, ...}
  note over API
    Response includes note_id so frontend can reference it in subsequent edits (PUT /api/notes/{note_id}).
    No password fields, no internal timestamps, clean DTO boundary.
  end note
else Authorization failed (JWT expired/invalid)
  EDITOR --> API : 1.2' POST with invalid JWT
  API --> EDITOR : 4.1' 401 Unauthorized
  EDITOR --> U : Redirect to login
end

== Phase 7: Frontend Update ==
EDITOR -> EDITOR : 5.1 Receive {note_id, created_at, ...}
EDITOR --> EDITOR : 5.2 Update state: note_id (now editable at /api/notes/{note_id}),\nShow "Saved" indicator
EDITOR --> U : 5.3 Note appears in sidebar list,\nEditor shows success

note across
  Latency target: < 200ms (API) from 1.2 to 4.1.
  - 1.3-1.4: Auth (JWT decode) ~5ms
  - 2.1-2.3: Folder lookup ~30ms
  - 3.1: Aggregate creation ~1ms
  - 3.2-3.3: Database INSERT ~50ms
  - 3.4: DTO conversion ~1ms
  - Total backend: ~87ms ✓
end note

@enduml
